# Column order on a real page.
#
# The expected columns live in Configuration/pages/ContactForm.json rather than in this script: a
# column list is a property of the page, so a renamed or reordered column is one edit to the page
# file instead of one edit per case that touches the grid.
#
# These grids sit in expansion panels far down the page. Creatio fills a panel only once it scrolls
# into view, so reaching them is the framework's job, not the script's: 'check' opens and scrolls to
# the panel named by the grid's label before it reads anything.

use Supervisor
open ContactForm for c4ed336c-3e9b-40fe-8b82-5632476472b4

# Creatio reopens a page on the tab it was last left on, so the tab is stated rather than assumed.
click GeneralInfoTab

check AddressList exists
check AddressList columns

check CareerList exists
check CareerList columns

# On another tab, to show that reaching a grid is the framework's job wherever it lives.
click ServiceTab
check CasesList exists
check CasesList columns
